hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"656","Abu Kabash narrated: I brought a six-month-old goat to Madinah and suffered a loss, so I went to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and mentioned it to him. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""A sheep that is eight or nine months old is the best for sacrifice."""
"657","Sayyidah Umm Karz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say regarding ‘Aqiqah: “For a boy, two goats and for a girl, one goat (should be slaughtered). It does not matter to you whether they are male or female.”"
"658","Sayyida Umm Karz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: She asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about ‘Aqiqah. So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “For a boy, two goats; and for a girl, one goat. And it does not matter to you whether they (the goats) are male or female.”"
"659","Sayyida Umm Bani Karz Ka'bain (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say regarding 'Aqiqah: ""For a boy, two equal (similar) goats, and for a girl, one goat (should be slaughtered)."""
"660","Sayyida Umm Karz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: ""For a boy, two 'aqiqahs (two animals) and for a girl, one 'aqiqah."""
"661","Lady Asma bint Yazid (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated: One day we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), when a vessel of water was presented to him. He (peace be upon him) drank from it, then ordered it to be given to them, so they drank. That vessel was passed to all those present. One of the attendees said: I am fasting. Among them, one person said: He fasts every day and never misses a day. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts continuously, (in the Shari'ah) he neither fasts nor breaks his fast."""
